From: Sam Pastoriza <pastorsj@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Report ontology resolution lineage

Chat results gain resolution_lineage: each extracted phrase with the ontology
object, table and column it resolved to, taken from the retrieved column
attributes. Scores, embeddings, prompts and reasoning stay out.

Upstream: NVIDIA/auto-ontology#251 and #256.
---
diff --git a/auto_ontology/retrieval/data_access/semantic_search.py b/auto_ontology/retrieval/data_access/semantic_search.py
index 40c12ab7..d34cd330 100644
--- a/auto_ontology/retrieval/data_access/semantic_search.py
+++ b/auto_ontology/retrieval/data_access/semantic_search.py
@@ -305,7 +305,18 @@ def _hits_to_semantic_rows(
             "label": lab,
             "score": score,
         }
-        for _field in ("name", "schema_name", "database_name", "data_type", "source"):
+        # The term, table and column let callers show which catalog objects a
+        # question resolved to (see ``text_to_sql.main._resolution_lineage``).
+        for _field in (
+            "name",
+            "term_name",
+            "table_name",
+            "source_column",
+            "schema_name",
+            "database_name",
+            "data_type",
+            "source",
+        ):
             val = meta.get(_field)
             if val is not None:
                 row[_field] = val
